==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|leygʰ-|to bind|lang=la}}<ref>Pokorny 668</ref>. Cf. Middle Low German {{term|lik|līk|lang=gml}}, Old Norse {{term|lík|lang=non}}. Possibly related to Middle High German {{term|geleich||joint|lang=gmh}}, whence modern German {{term|gleich|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈli.ɡoː/|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|ligō|ligonis|ligōnis|m|third}}

# A [[hoe]], [[mattock]]

